ame  30-minute sessions for the sake of  efficiency  in order to shorten the uat accordingly  i helped with condensing and eliminating  some questions in the uat form and  smartsheet  with these changes made we found that  these 30-minute sessions worked  wonderfully during our second round of  uat  furthermore ohsu and cognitive fix the  app so that additional labs now show for  live patients  i got to help with checking the app's  logs in order to track down what errors  were occurring within the app  during the process of getting this fixed  i did a fair amount of testing the app  so i could ensure things had been fixed  especially for some of the more  complicated patients  testing the app involved being pretty  well versed in epic for example i would  check to see if the labs in the  patient's epic chart matched with those  showing in the app and that they were  showing all the results that they should  have been  i did extensive testing with several  different patients in order to test the  app to the fullest extent  both with patricia noel and poc and with  several real patients in production  with the real patients i found some  inconsistencies between the app and epic  and compiled them into a spreadsheet and  then made a word doc with screenshots  and notes on the problems both of which  helped with debugging the app  a lot of the problems that i found  relating to data missing from the app  have been due to problems with  fireworking improperly as fire is still  a relatively new tool  and here's a snippet of the excel  spreadsheet that i was talking about  except without the patient medical  record numbers or mrns showing because  those are easily identifiable  i would show you the aforementioned  screenshots and notes document but it  has a lot of personal health information  and it would be hard to adequately  redact  future steps future steps for this  project include continuing to conduct  uat with more providers from  pre-selected clinics and having 